        <updated>2026-09-29T19:58:44.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25351731?u=c0ece93f0dabf1e298253953d28aa0f097ffa072&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Reran the collector tests on every Bun release from 1.0.0 to 1.4.2 and this fixes the entries that were off.</p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">fetch()</code> and <code class="notranslate">Request</code> taking a <code class="notranslate">ReadableStream</code> body landed in 1.1.39, <code class="notranslate">WebAssembly.compileStreaming()</code> / <code class="notranslate">instantiateStreaming()</code> in 1.2.20 (was 1.2.18), and the <code class="notranslate">SubtleCrypto</code> encapsulate/decapsulate methods, <code class="notranslate">getPublicKey()</code> and <code class="notranslate">supports()</code> in 1.4.0.</p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">FormData.append()</code> filename support goes back to 1.0.0, but the collector's test uses an empty <code class="notranslate">Blob</code>, which lost its name until 1.4.1. I left a note instead of using 1.4.1.</p>]]></content>
